  "implemented": [
    "Fresh typed PArrangement-to-PArrangeSetup version-8 decoding preserves source object identities and raw Float32 base-rate / Double factor bits without scanning for a plausible rate.",
    "Current V5 imports initialize the editable application sample rate only from an admitted saved configuration. Frozen V1-V4 interpretation, original CPR and historical reports remain unchanged.",
    "An explicit saved-project-clock source-event mode replays preserved configuration independently of the current editable Rebase rate; raw source configuration travels with the ephemeral playback result.",
    "The admitted source context requires an integral base rate from 10000 to 192000 Hz and exact positive-one factor. Missing/unknown/unsupported configuration cannot silently become a native rate.",
    "Existing native placement, reader/accessor ownership, source capacity, processing and provenance gates remain enforced. The explicit supplied-Rebase-clock and source-rate modes remain separate."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Saved configuration is not a measurement of effective hosted, engine or device rate. Mutable providers, post-read callbacks and nonunity factors remain outside this interpretation.",
    "Native out-of-range fallback to 44100, unchecked nonfinite values, other setup versions and unsupported embedded datums are not admitted by the narrower application policy.",
    "Different source/output clocks can change speed, pitch and physical source-time consumption. No transparent resampler is silently inserted, and incomplete source reads remain rejected.",
    "Own GUI/engine observations and analytical/static controls are not DAC capture, native callback equivalence or Cubase runtime output.",
    "Full-project MIDI/plugin/routing/mixer/automation behavior, arbitrary nested events and complete product fidelity remain unestablished."
  ]
